@Gateway_HostAddress = http://localhost:5000
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@orderId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### 1. Gateway Forwarding -> Catalog API: GET all products
# Forwarded to http://localhost:5001/products via /catalog prefix removal
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/catalog/products
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Gateway Forwarding -> Catalog API: GET all categories
# Forwarded to http://localhost:5001/categories via /catalog prefix removal
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/catalog/categories
Accept: application/json

###

### 3. Gateway Forwarding -> Catalog API: GET single product
# Forwarded to http://localhost:5001/products/{{productId}}
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/catalog/products/{{productId}}
Accept: application/json

###

### 4. Gateway Forwarding -> Order API: POST Create Order
# Forwarded directly to http://localhost:5002/orders
POST {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customerEmail": "customer@example.com",
  "items": [
    {
      "productId": "{{productId}}",
      "quantity": 1
    }
  ]
}

###

### 5. Gateway Forwarding -> Order API: GET order by ID
# Forwarded to http://localhost:5002/orders/{{orderId}}
GET {{Gateway_HostAddress}}/orders/{{orderId}}
Accept: application/json

###
